# Tech Research: BMAD first-use directory creation in a project that never had BMAD (issue 478, BMAD half only)

## Task Overview

On 2026-11-07 the user decided that BMAD SHOULD create its needed directories on first use in a project that never had it. This supersedes, for first-use creation only, the 2026-09-25 owner decision OD-1 ("BMad is installed per project only, never globally") and the related non-goals. Global installation of BMAD itself is NOT requested. Today, in a Coder AIDev02 workspace, the `bmad` slug installer (`templates/VSCode-AIDev02/image/catalogue/bmad/install.sh`) installs BMAD only into the seed repo; in any other project nothing is created and `bmad-*` skills do not exist, so the user cannot start BMAD without knowing the one-command manual install. Tests `.github/contract-tests/test-57-catalogue-configure.sh` and `.github/contract-tests/test-startup-boot.sh` pin "no seed means BMAD writes nothing".

This task is a documentation-only technical investigation (tech-research skill, Standard depth, QA intensity standard). It runs 5 codebase research agents, 2 web research agents, 4 synthesis agents and five QA gates (3, 3, 7, 3 and 3 report-only agents respectively, each gate followed by one fix agent and a verification round), and produces ONE deliverable: `RESEARCH-REPORT-bmad-first-use.md` in this task folder, with findings, gap analysis, options with effort and risk, a recommendation, and an implementation plan that names every pinned test and every document that must change. The report feeds (1) `.dev/issues/478/spec.md`, written by the orchestrator after this research, and (2) `/sc:workflow` to produce an implementation plan. No product code is changed by this task.

## Key Objectives

The following objectives MUST be achieved by this task:

1. **Establish verified facts about real BMAD 6.9.0 behaviour:** what `bmad install` creates in a project that never had BMAD, what an installed skill needs at run time, whether any code consumes `global_target_dir` (user-scope skill install), and what happens when `_bmad/` is absent. Every fact carries file and line evidence from `/opt/nvm/versions/node/v24.22.2/lib/node_modules/bmad-method/` or is marked UNVERIFIED.
2. **Map the repo surfaces that a first-use mechanism would touch:** the image-wide `bmad` CLI wrapper, the catalogue `bmad` slug (install.sh, manifest.yaml, module.tf), profiles, startup flow, HOME persistence, user-level Claude Code surfaces (`~/.claude/settings.json`, `~/.claude/skills/`), and whether `superclaude install` would overwrite a user-level hook or skill.
3. **List every pinned test assertion and every document** that states or pins "no seed means BMAD writes nothing" or the per-project-only rule, and say for each candidate option which assertion breaks and what the new assertion would be.
4. **Compare at least options A-F** (document only; user-level bootstrap skill; image CLI wrapper; Claude Code user-level hook; home-level `bmad install`; upstream user-scope install) with effort, risk, reuse, files affected, pros and cons, and recommend one.
5. **State feasibility plainly:** if the evidence shows the ask cannot be met without a global BMAD install or a change in another repo (IronClaude or IronOrca), Sections 7 and 9 of the report must say so explicitly so the orchestrator can STOP and re-scope.
6. **Deliver a report that passes five QA gates** (research completeness with 3 agents, synthesis quality with 3, report validation with 7 lenses, source-document fidelity with 3 agents, anti-omission with 3 agents) with serialized fixes, and carry the two owner-reading ambiguities (user-level stub allowed? what counts as "first use"?) into Open Questions without guessing.

